OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F388A1785334695
OL,3,CCriminal Cases Review Commission told
OL,4,Cto deal with Fordingbridge rape
OL,5,Csentences
OL,7,FThe boys were given non-custodial
OL,8,Fsentences in May after a judge at
OL,9,FSouthampton Crown Court said he should
OL,10,F"avoid criminalising these children
OL,11,Funnecessarily" and that detention was
OL,12,Fa "last resort".
OL,14,FThe two older boys were involved in
OL,15,Fboth attacks while the 14-year-old
OL,16,Fencouraged the rape of the second
OL,17,Fvictim.
OL,26,@rD@AOUsD@NO]tD@COUtD@OO]
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G5/8
